ns in Canada and the U.S. Midwest, plus wealth management and capital markets. Revenue (net interest income plus noninterest income) rose 10.6% to C$36.3B in fiscal 2025 (ended Oct 31, 2025). Net interest income rose 10.4% to C$21.5B and noninterest income rose 11.0% to C$14.8B; noninterest expense rose 8.2%, and the provision for credit losses was C$3.6B, versus C$3.8B.","Net income to common rose 19.3% to C$8.3B, or C$11.44 per diluted share, and the efficiency ratio was 58.2% versus 59.5%. BMO returned C$8.4B through dividends and buybacks."],"highlights":["Revenue rose 10.6% to C$36.3B.","Net interest income rose 10.4%.","Noninterest income rose 11.0%.","Net income to common rose 19.3% to C$8.3B."],"watch":["Net loans fell 0.1% to C$677.2B.","Net interest income depends on interest rates.","Noninterest expense was C$21.1B, up 8.2%.","Credit-loss provision was C$3.6B."],"table":[["Total revenue",36.274,32.795,1],["Net interest income",21.487,19.468],["Noninterest income",14.787,13.327],["Noninterest expense",21.107,19.499],["Provision for credit losses",3.617,3.761],["Pre-tax income",11.55,9.535,1],["Income tax",2.825,2.208],["Noncontrolling interests",-0.016,-0.009],["Preferred dividends & other",-0.436,0.386],["Net income to common",8.273,6.932,1],["Diluted EPS (C$)",11.44,9.51,0,"eps"],["Book value per share (C$)",122.020464,112.675348,0,"eps"]],"sources":[["Bank of Montreal Form 40-F filings (SEC EDGAR)","https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0000927971&type=40-F"],["BMO financial statements (StockAnalysis)","https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/bmo/financials/"]]},"video":{"revenueLine":{"cap":"Net interest income was 59% of revenue.","say":"Net interest income made up 59 percent of revenue."},"spotlights":[{"kicker":"Revenue","big":"C$36.3B","sub":"revenue · +10.6%","lines":["Net interest income C$21.5B","Noninterest income C$14.8B"],"cap":"Revenue rose 10.6% to C$36.3B.","say":"Revenue rose 10.6% to C$36.3B."},{"kicker":"Per share","bi